    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 **30 tests, 0 failures, BUILD SUCCESS**, including the new `Cp19Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the daily owner-creation limit (reject with 429 when 100+ owners already exist for today by `registrationDate`), following the existing per-city limit pattern already in the codebase.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`DailyOwnerLimitExceededException.java`** (new) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` carrying the day and limit, mirroring `CityOwnerLimitExceededException`.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 in `addOwner`, after `registrationDate` is defaulted to today, added a `rejectDailyLimitReached(owner.getRegistrationDate())` call. The new `rejectDailyLimitReached` method counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals the new owner's date and throws when the count reaches the `DAILY_OWNER_LIMIT` (100). The count is taken pre-persist, so it excludes the owner being created.\n\n3. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`** \u2014 added an `@ExceptionHandler` that maps `DailyOwnerLimitExceededException` to **HTTP 429 (TOO_MANY_REQUESTS)** with a `ProblemDetail` body, consistent with the other handlers.\n\nThe rejection is applied on the create endpoint (`POST /api/owners`); the update path is unaffected, matching the spec's \"creating an owner\" wording.",
